Helios DXVK fork: NVK composed-Present sources wait for the KMD's read claim

Conduit guest/windows/docs/zero-copy-present.md 24.10.3. With KMD BltAsync
the windowed Blt that copies a composed Present's source may still be
queued when Present returns, and the KMD claims the source's resource id in
the read ledger until the copy retires. Nothing else orders the next NVK
render into that swap-chain buffer after the copy (NVK submits on its own
RM channel, which dxgkrnl does not schedule).

- DxvkImage::heliosBltSourceResid / setHeliosBltSourceResid: the UMD tags a
  Present's source with its ledger id (NVK's IMPORT_RM id, which is also the
  KMD's resource id of the adopted allocation).
- heliosEmitScanoutReuseWaits qualifies tagged images too and uses the tag
  as the ledger id (an NVK allocation has no Venus id to ask for), so a
  command list touching the source waits GPU-side for the claim to retire,
  exactly as for a scanout buffer.

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp
index 49553a9b..3c0150ee 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp
@@ -9906,9 +9906,14 @@ namespace dxvk {
       const auto& info = image->info();
 
       // Only images the host can read back: the direct-OPTIMAL primary, the
-      // exact-primary LINEAR shape, and the KMD-owned LINEAR fallback target.
-      // dwm's compositing SRVs and ordinary backbuffers never qualify.
-      if (!info.heliosDirectOptimalScanout
+      // exact-primary LINEAR shape, the KMD-owned LINEAR fallback target, and
+      // (NVK) the source of a composed Present, which the KMD's Blt copy may
+      // still be reading after Present returned (KMD BltAsync, Conduit
+      // zero-copy-present.md 24.10.3). dwm's compositing SRVs never qualify.
+      const uint32_t bltResid = image->heliosBltSourceResid();
+
+      if (!bltResid
+       && !info.heliosDirectOptimalScanout
        && !info.heliosScanoutPrimary
        && !info.heliosLinearScanoutTarget)
         continue;
@@ -9917,13 +9922,15 @@ namespace dxvk {
       // rotate_resource_backings swaps storages between images, so the
       // create-time id goes stale while the storage's backing memory is
       // authoritative (the 56th-session lesson, restated by the spec §5.1).
+      // An NVK Blt source has no backing rotation (one dedicated allocation
+      // whose IMPORT_RM id is the ledger key) and no Venus id to ask for.
       Rc<DxvkResourceAllocation> storage = image->storage();
 
       if (storage == nullptr)
         continue;
 
-      const uint32_t resid = helios_acquire::residFromMemory(
-        storage->getMemoryInfo().memory);
+      const uint32_t resid = bltResid ? bltResid
+        : helios_acquire::residFromMemory(storage->getMemoryInfo().memory);
 
       if (!resid) {
         m_heliosScanoutResidMiss += 1u;
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_image.h b/src/dxvk/dxvk_image.h
